---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Src from '../components/Src.astro';
import Aff from '../components/Aff.astro';
import { S } from '../data/sources.js';
const title = 'Virtual Mailbox Check Deposit Fees Compared: Free, $3, $4.95 or $10 a Check';
const description = 'What it costs to have a virtual mailbox deposit a paper check: US Global Mail (no handling fee), Stable (from $3/check), Traveling Mailbox ($4.95 + postage), iPostal1 ($4.95 per 5 checks), Earth Class Mail ($10, or $39/mo for 5). From each provider\'s own page.';
const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":title,"description":description,"dateModified":"2026-11-20"};
---
<Base title={title} description={description} updated="2026-11-20" schema={schema}>
  <h1>Virtual mailbox check deposit fees, compared</h1>
  <p class="lede">If customers or clients still mail you paper checks, the deposit fee can cost more than the mailbox itself. Usually the provider endorses the check and mails it to your bank, and you pay a handling fee plus postage. Here's what each provider publishes, as of November 20, 2026.</p>

  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Handling fee</th><th>Plus</th><th>How it's deposited</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>US Global Mail</strong></td><td>None. "We don't charge any additional handling fees for check deposit" <Src href={S.usgmCheck} /></td><td>Standard shipping (trackable methods only), and optional repacking <Src href={S.usgmCheck} /></td><td>They print a deposit slip and mail the check to your bank. Or you deposit the scanned image through your bank yourself <Src href={S.usgmCheck} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Stable</strong></td><td>"Volume-based plans as low as $3/check" <Src href={S.stable} /></td><td>A separate check-deposit purchase; "you must have an existing Stable account" <Src href={S.stable} /></td><td>Electronic and mail-in options <Src href={S.stable} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Traveling Mailbox</strong></td><td>$4.95 per check <Src href={S.tmb} /></td><td>Postage <Src href={S.tmb} /></td><td>Endorsed "For Deposit Only" and mailed to your bank <Src href={S.tmb} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>iPostal1</strong></td><td>$4.95 to deposit up to 5 checks (most locations) <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td><td>"The cost of check scan(s) and trackable shipping." U.S. only <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td><td>By mail <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Earth Class Mail</strong> (LegalZoom Virtual Mail)</td><td>$10 per check without a subscription. Or the check deposit subscription: $39/mo with 5 checks included, then $2 per check <Src href={S.ecm} /></td><td>Expedited: $20 per check, with free overnight shipping to Bank of America, JPMorgan Chase and Wells Fargo. Other deposits go by USPS <Src href={S.ecm} /></td><td>Mailed to your bank <Src href={S.ecm} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>PostScan Mail</strong></td><td>Not listed on the pricing page <Src href={S.psm} /></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Anytime Mailbox</strong></td><td>Set by each location's operator <Src href={S.atm} /></td><td></td><td>Listed as a service on location pages <Src href={S.atmOmaha} /></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <p>Want your own number? The <a href="/virtual-mailbox-chooser/">virtual mailbox chooser</a> works out a monthly cost for your mail volume, scans and checks.</p>

  <h2>What three checks a month costs</h2>
  <p>Handling fees only. Postage or shipping is extra everywhere except where noted, and it depends on the carrier you pick.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>3 checks, mailed together</th><th>Math</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>US Global Mail</td><td><strong>$0</strong> + shipping</td><td>No handling fee <Src href={S.usgmCheck} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>iPostal1</td><td><strong>$4.95</strong> + scans + shipping</td><td>One $4.95 deposit covers up to 5 checks. The page doesn't say how scans of checks are charged <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Stable</td><td><strong>from $9</strong></td><td>3 × "as low as $3." The rate at low volume isn't published <Src href={S.stable} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Traveling Mailbox</td><td><strong>$14.85</strong> + postage</td><td>3 × $4.95 <Src href={S.tmb} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Earth Class Mail</td><td><strong>$30</strong>, or <strong>$39</strong> on the subscription</td><td>3 × $10 without a subscription. The $39 subscription only pays off from the 4th check a month (4 × $10 = $40) <Src href={S.ecm} /></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Things to check before relying on mailed deposits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Will your bank take checks by mail?</strong> US Global Mail tells customers to call their local branch first and ask, "Do you accept checks by mail?" <Src href={S.usgmCheck} /></li>
    <li><strong>Mobile deposit from a scan</strong> depends on your bank's own rules. US Global Mail offers it as an option <Src href={S.usgmCheck} />, but whether your bank accepts a deposit from a scanned image is up to the bank.</li>
    <li><strong>The deposit fee usually comes on top of your plan.</strong> Earth Class Mail lists the check deposit subscription ($39/mo) separately from its MailBox plans, which start at $39/mo <Src href={S.ecm} />. LegalZoom's FAQ now says check depositing "can be added for an additional fee" <Src href={S.lzVm} />, so 5 checks a month on the Starter plan costs $78 a month in total (rechecked 2026-11-21). Full fee list: <a href="/earth-class-mail-pricing/">Earth Class Mail pricing</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Choosing a provider for other reasons too? See the <a href="/virtual-mailbox-pricing-comparison/">full price table</a>, <a href="/virtual-mailbox-for-llc/">virtual mailboxes for an LLC</a>, and <a href="/traveling-mailbox-vs-postscan-mail/">Traveling Mailbox vs PostScan Mail</a>.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><Aff id="usglobalmail" href="https://www.usglobalmail.com?via=michelle" text="US Global Mail" /></li>
    <li><Aff id="travelingmailbox" href="https://www.travelingmailbox.com/" text="Traveling Mailbox" /></li>
    <li><Aff id="ipostal1" href="https://ipostal1.com/" text="iPostal1" /></li>
  </ul>
  <p><a href="/">Mailbox Atlas home</a></p>
</Base>
